o the active context's [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]glossary note expands with #memory/glossary while bare #glossary [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]remains unresolved.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]xprompt_memories.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/xprompt_memories.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-hf[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-hf/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Shared xprompt-memory layout and catalog contract[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]shared-memory-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared-memory-contract: define memory source precedence, reference [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]naming, type metadata, and native editor/catalog behavior in the Rust [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]core.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Python discovery and expansion integration[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]python-memory-runtime[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shared-memory-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]python-memory-runtime: consume the shared contract, load valid memory [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes as contextual xprompts, and enforce memory namespace semantics.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]CLI, ACE, helper, and editor presentation[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-user-surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after python-memory-runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-user-surfaces: expose xprompt-memory identity and refresh [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]behavior consistently across every xprompt discovery and authoring [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]surface.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory documentation and glossary regeneration[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after python-memory-runtime[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-docs: document explicit xprompt-memory inclusion, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]glossary term, and regenerate managed memory outputs through sase memory[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]init.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cross-runtime verification[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]xprompt-memory-verification[dim] · [dim][/dim]after memory-user-surfaces, memory-docs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]xprompt-memory-verification: prove contextual precedence, namespaced [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expansion, catalog parity, memory regeneration, and absence of dynamic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]matching end to end.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-hf","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-hf.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-91b620c8132da81986fa95ab12bd3028","started_at":"2026-08-08T12:51:21.385211+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"eeb408df2b17bca29e64018e7c912852cf76e36abccc3e23c97280653391cc64","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-hf.5/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"a8a78f45fa832eb722af28575793a2f385f700366011f9cdd0d359391a6cd9fd","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-hf.5/meta.json","size_bytes":600},"prompt":{"digest":"fecf3226a59f7e6df8f35788dd6b8827eddf812a10783179b21acdf39969d760","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-